community_join.s:
outcome: people join and leave communities, and member counts are real.
1. migrations/0003_members.sql:
-- cm community member: c community, u user, t joined ms
create table cm (c text not null references c (i) on delete cascade, u text not null references u (i) on delete cascade, t integer not null, primary key (c, u)) without rowid;
create index cm_u on cm (u);
insert or ignore into cm (c, u, t) select i, u, t from c;
update c set m = (select count(*) from cm where cm.c = c.i);
2. db.ts: insert_comm also adds the creator to cm; `set_member(d, user_id, comm_id, on)` changes cm and recounts c.m in one batch; comm_by_slug takes the viewer and adds `j` (j = viewer joined, commented).
3. POST /api/communities/[name]/join `{ o }` (o = on). src/routes/c/[communityName]/+page.svelte shows the member count and a join/leave button.
4. smoke: B joins A's community, member_count is 2; B leaves, it is 1.
